// Locate Animals or Plants: `BuffKind::Detecting` applied to
// `SenseKind::Nature`, whose predicate matches `CreatureKind::Beast` *or*
// `CreatureKind::Plant` (`server/src/sys/detection.rs`) -- a direct
// mechanical fit for a spell that lets the caster choose either category.
// Simplified from the D&D original the same way every other spell in this
// family is: it reveals every matching creature in range rather than
// pulling toward one named kind, since the sense declaration carries no
// target descriptor.
//
// The D&D original's range is 5 miles, which has no sane literal conversion
// for a bounded spatial query -- deliberately scaled down to 300 m instead,
// the same magnitude the "locate" family (`locate_object.ron`/
// `locate_creature.ron`) already uses for their own (smaller, ~1000 ft)
// D&D ranges, rather than inventing a third distance tier for one spell.
//
// Sheet duration is `Instant`; `duration: Some(1.0)` here is a plumbing
// formality exactly like `identify.ron`'s own -- a `BuffData` needs a
// nonzero duration for at least one tick to exist and be revealed/synced at
// all, and one second is long enough for that single reveal to land on the
// client before the buff (and the `Detected` entry) expires. This is a
// one-shot flash of insight, not an ongoing sense.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(
            kind: Detecting,
            data: BuffData(
                strength: 0.0,
                duration: Some(1.0),
                misc_data: Some(Sense(Nature, 300.0, Snapshot)),
            ),
        ),
    ],
    energy_cost: 20,
    enforced_limit: false,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Divination),
        source: Some(Primordial),
        // level 2 spell -> min_level 12, same `level * 6` convention
        // see_invisibility.ron/true_seeing.ron derive from every other
        // shipped spell that sets this field.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(12)),
    ),
)
